---
description: "Repo-wide consistency sweep. Aligns naming, docstring style, log fields, error message phrasing, and removes dead code."
---

# /polish

## Canonical algorithm

1. Resolve scope: default = entire `src/eawf/`; `--scope=<dir|file>`
   narrows.
2. Sweep checks: naming, docstrings, log fields, error message
   phrasing, dead code, citation density, draft sentinels, scrub status.
3. Apply fixes inline. If a change touches public API, stop and ask.

## Options

- `--scope=<dir|file>` — narrow the sweep from the default entire
  `src/eawf/` to one directory or file.
- `--auto-apply-safe` — explicitly auto-apply the small "safe" subset
  (formatting, comment phrasing) for this invocation.
- `--category naming|docstrings|logs|errors|dead-code` — filter the
  sweep to one check category. Default is all categories.

## Pre-flight checklist

- [ ] Scope is declared and bounded.
- [ ] No public API rename without explicit user confirmation.
- [ ] The target iter is NOT yet closed. Iter close is gated on
      `audit + polish + ship CI + PR review pass` per the
      `iter-phase-close-timing` rule in AGENTS.md; `/polish` runs
      after `/audit` and before that close.

## Decision surfaces

Public-API renames and dead-code deletions MUST be raised via
`AskUserQuestion` (options: `apply` / `defer-to-backlog` / `skip`)
instead of asking in free text. No persisted config bypasses this
protected decision.

## Output contract

Skill envelope with a change list grouped by category and a deferred-
items list for changes needing user OK.

